es flashrom search for an fmap and add its regions earlier. The follow-up patch introduces a command-line option which depends on this behavior.  BUG=chromium:635241 BRANCH=none TEST=tested with follow-up patch  Change-Id: I763f4dcdd5ab6d947ad59776931f42d31c2a253c Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405109 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405109" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/09/405109/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I11b926788a88a07fb9a05f1ed0c88c07c6a82c21" commit="5c84e74c045d99cd45c0c20f1d8d012471504534" commit_message="platform_MemCheck: Remove memory free check  We have an assumption that the half memory should be free just after reboot the machine. This probably isn't true anymore after we start enable ARC++ in the board with 2GB of memory. This CL removes this assuption from platform_MemCheck test.  BUG=chromium:660202 TEST=Tested in minnie. Result does not in clude memory free.  Change-Id: I11b926788a88a07fb9a05f1ed0c88c07c6a82c21 Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/404971 Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="404971" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/71/404971/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id5a7d666c204b37601febc2710f54aa289c64e62" commit="8be6747ff4e6fac8dea2fac9c455c7fc7e5ed34e" commit_message="power: fix declarations of string array constant  String array constants should be declared as 'const char* const[]' but not 'const char*[]'. The latter is an array of &quot;mutable&quot; pointers to constant string literal.  BUG=None TEST=Build and run unit tests.  Change-Id: Id5a7d666c204b37601febc2710f54aa289c64e62 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/404992 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="404992" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/92/404992/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iad57c67f8e3028e7a37b24e2203157726009ee1a" commit="be5a1b24c45f15a8f2c9a893dc93e954643c5021" commit_message="cros-disks: fix declarations of string array constant  String array constants should be declared as 'const char* const[]' but not 'const char*[]'. The latter is an array of &quot;mutable&quot; pointers to constant string literal.  BUG=None TEST=Build and run unit tests.  Change-Id: Iad57c67f8e3028e7a37b24e2203157726009ee1a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/404557 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="404557" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/57/404557/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I98c8682ac6d46e7a3bc0c2aa85e5024915989aef" commit="27287f11f1268c1fe41d2ab24e4a962f5f8b17fb" commit_message="[autotest] Fix argparse handling of arguments starting with dashes  BUG=chromium:658013 TEST=Run test_that against lab  Change-Id: I98c8682ac6d46e7a3bc0c2aa85e5024915989aef Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402710 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="402710" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/10/402710/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Iaa073ec11dabed7265620d370fcd01ea8c0c2054" commit="d1d37d0d7124c9bf0932f63957f1436cdac07483" commit_message="arm64: arm_tf: Do not build raw bl31.bin binary  Coreboot's build system picks up the BL31 image as an ELF from the ARM Trusted Firmware submodule and inserts it into CBFS. However, the generic 'bl31' build target we run in the ARM Trusted Firmware build system also generates a raw bl31.bin binary file.  We don't need that binary, and with the recently added support for multiple non-contiguous program segments in BL31 it can grow close to 4GB in size (by having one section mapped near the start and one near the end of the address space). To avoid clogging up people's hard drives with 4GB of zeroes, let's only build the target we actually need.  BRANCH=gru BUG=chrome-os-partner:56314 TEST=FEATURES=noclean emerge-kevin coreboot, confirm that there's no giant build/3rdparty/arm-trusted-firmware/bl31.bin file left in the build artifacts.  Change-Id: Iaa073ec11dabed7265620d370fcd01ea8c0c2054 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405110 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="405110" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/10/405110/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If1b6e88192ad0a59b19b6b6b664b46780596fa18" commit="f2ed382358b69edbac1b27b12128d727b458022b" commit_message="Pyro: Add firmware for shipping mode follow Pyro battery spec.  Add firmware for shipping mode follow Pyro battery spec.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=The battery could enter shipping mode and wake up  Change-Id: If1b6e88192ad0a59b19b6b6b664b46780596fa18 Signed-off-by: Bruce.Wan &lt;Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403731 Commit-Ready: Keith Tzeng &lt;keith.tzeng@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: Keith Tzeng &lt;keith.tzeng@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="403731" owner_email="Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/31/403731/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I542e630732e74aa59c045b7891a97566cf4a3b2d" commit="83bc1d9e448ddc016dd4ae869fe54f39e601df47" commit_message="init: use frecon pipes instead of tty  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57359 BRANCH=None TEST=perform normal-&gt;dev transition CQ-DEPEND=CL:401477  Change-Id: I542e630732e74aa59c045b7891a97566cf4a3b2d Signed-off-by: Shelley Chen &lt;shchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402008 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="402008" owner_email="shchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/08/402008/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2f128f062ec4947e68b064ca643ffad18643b46d" commit="089f74bae8f701fd753bb12b26bdd2af7ef099ee" commit_message="auto_updater: raise exception when stateful update fails to clean tmp files.  Current auto_updater has a bug: it checks whether the tmp files exist after stateful update, but with a wrong cmd. Those cmd will always return 0 as return code, which will miss raising exceptions.  This CL changes cmd from 'test -f $file; echo $?' to 'test -f $file'.  BUG=chromium:659385 TEST=run repair with local autotest and devserver.  Change-Id: I2f128f062ec4947e68b064ca643ffad18643b46d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/403191 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="403191" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/91/403191/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ibe98884e8291053052131ea539860da266666c26" commit="a1b82426ae80e553e308d17e6373043cade1359c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ath10k: refactor ath10k_dbg().  Only enable trace event when debug mask is set to avoid export internal symbols.  BUG=None TEST=None Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@chromium.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ibe98884e8291053052131ea539860da266666c26 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/395088 Commit-Ready: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="395088" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/88/395088/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id9ae0fb174cfe382ec30a1175f54c0891543c4